user_message:
Review every unordered pair using local zero-based indices, not hypothesis IDs.
Preserve all feature fields and report exact pending alignment differences.

[
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 23,
    "feature": {
      "name": "any_comment_specific_verifiable_procedural_example",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "OC_comments"
      ],
      "definition": "Any counter-argument comment in OC_comments: cites at least one specific, verifiable procedural example (a concrete named or checkable process, rule, procedure, case or step-by-step mechanism of how something is actually done)",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read the OC_comments JSON list (comments by users other than the OP; order carries no meaning). Return 1 if at least one comment gives a specific, verifiable procedural example: a concrete, checkable description of how a particular process, legal/institutional procedure, protocol, rule or workflow actually operates or operated (e.g. a named statute's steps, a specific court procedure, a documented practice), that could be checked against an external source. Generic hypotheticals, abstract principles, vague appeals to 'how things work', and personal opinions without a checkable procedure do not count. Quoted OP text does not count. Return 0 if all comments are assessable and none contain such an example. Return null if OC_comments is missing, unparseable or empty."
    }
  },
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 69,
    "feature": {
      "name": "any_comment_cites_specific_localized_example",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "OC_comments"
      ],
      "definition": "Any OC_comments comment: cites at least one specific, localized example (a particular named/identifiable case, instance, event, person, place or concrete situation) as part of its counter-argument.",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read the JSON list in OC_comments (comments by users other than the OP). Return 1 if at least one comment cites a specific, localized example in support of its counter-argument: a particular identifiable case, event, person, place, organization, study instance or concrete situation (e.g. a named country's policy, a specific incident, a personal anecdote with concrete particulars). Return 0 if all comments are assessable and none cites such an example; purely general claims, abstract reasoning, hypotheticals without a particular case, and generic category references do not count. Do not require that the example be correct or persuasive. Quoted text from the OP does not count. Return null if OC_comments is missing, empty-unparseable, or not a valid list. Do not use any other column."
    }
  },
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 71,
    "feature": {
      "name": "any_comment_concrete_checkable_example",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "OC_comments"
      ],
      "definition": "Any counter-argument comment in OC_comments: contains at least one concrete, specific, checkable example (named/particular case, event, data point, study, source or link, or observable instance) offered as support, rather than only abstract principles.",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read OC_comments (JSON list of comments by users other than OP; order carries no meaning). Return 1 if at least one comment itself offers a concrete, specific example that a reader could check (e.g., a named person/event/place/law/study, specific figure, link/citation, or a particular verifiable instance) as support for its point. Return 0 if the comments are assessable and none contains such an example (only abstract principles, generic hypotheticals, or vague unnamed appeals like 'many people'). Examples quoted from the OP do not count unless the commenter adds their own. Do not read conversation or any later replies. Return null if OC_comments is missing, unparseable, or an empty list. Only the commenter's own text is used; no outcome information."
    }
  },
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 82,
    "feature": {
      "name": "any_comment_specific_example",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "OC_comments"
      ],
      "definition": "Any counter-argument comment in OC_comments: uses at least one specific, concrete illustrative example (1/0)",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read OC_comments (JSON list of comments by users other than the OP). Return 1 if at least one comment employs a specific, concrete illustrative example to support its point, e.g. a named person, event, case, study, product, or a detailed concrete scenario/instance. Vague generalities, abstract claims, purely hypothetical gestures without concrete detail ('e.g. someone might...'), and examples only quoted from the OP's text do not count. Return 0 if the list is parseable and no comment does. Return null if OC_comments is missing, empty, or unparseable. Do not use any other column."
    }
  }
]

Submit {"comparisons": [...]} covering every pair with a verdict and reason.
